# SYNTHETIC (Phase 2). Shape modeled on the real aclanthology.org/raw.githubusercontent.com
# 404 body (research/site-survey/acl-anthology.md §5 [LIVE]: Hugo-generated site-wide 404
# page, Content-Length 8019, identical body whether the missing path is a paper landing
# page or robots.txt). HttpClient maps 404 -> gone. The adapter reclassifies this in THREE
# distinct contexts, all exercised against this same fixture (design §6):
#   (a) primary bulk file missing ({year}.{venue}.xml AND the old-style candidate both
#       404) -> legal-empty (no proceedings that venue-year), not an error;
#   (b) findings companion file missing ({year}.findings.xml 404) -> legal-empty (no
#       Findings track that year), not an error;
#   (c) a PDF fetch 404 (early paper with no PDF, or a <removed>/<retracted> entry) -> gone
#       (resource terminal state, no reclassification -- this is the one context where the
#       404 legitimately IS an error/terminal-skip signal).
HTTP-STATUS: 404
Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8

<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><title>Not Found</title></head><body><p>404 The page you were looking for doesn't exist. Go back to the home page to browse the content of the Anthology, or try to use the search function (at the top) to find the content you were looking for.</p></body></html>
